        "id": 23720,
        "name": "Paul",
        "username": "Paul",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/paul/{size}/5862_2.png",
        "created_at": "2011-10-28T21:50:21.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;TheJayMann&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"TheJayMann\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Pretty much, every card is either a One-Shot, which means it’s discarded after play, or it’s not One-Shot, which means it remains in play after being played.  Titles such as Equipment, Ongoing, Device, or Minion are just there so they can be targeted by other cards (such as destroy all Equipment).</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>TheJayMann is totally correct!  Cards are either One-Shots, or not (as he stated), and the “not” category is further broken down between “Targets” and “Other” - the difference is that “targets” have HP and are destroyed if their current HP are reduced to 0 (or below), whereas non-target cards stay in play forever unless another card specifically says that it destroys them.</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:57:42.832Z",
